WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.787
Welcome to Module 9, Data Cleaning in PostgreSQL.

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:10.952
This module brings together the ideas from earlier modules and turns them into a repeatable cleaning workflow.

00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:18.057
We will profile missing and invalid values, standardize representation, validate business rules,

00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:22.487
identify duplicate groups, quarantine questionable records, preview updates safely,

00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:27.172
and add constraints when the rules are known.

00:00:27.172 --> 00:00:32.322
The most important principle is simple: cleaning should make uncertainty visible, not hide it.

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:37.397
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:37.397 --> 00:00:42.677
a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:47.942
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:51.717
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:58.887
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:58.887 --> 00:01:02.432
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:01:02.432 --> 00:01:06.542
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
